lz5-ex starts here. It is the extended line of LZ5, forked from the 1.5.1
maintenance release of the 1.5.0 code base. The API, the header names and the
block and frame formats are unchanged, so it stays drop-in compatible with LZ5
1.5.x. The entries below this line are the maintenance work that the fork is
based on. See README.md for what the "ex" is for.

v1.5.1 (maintenance release)
- fixed: high-compression tables (hashTable, hashTable3, chainTable) were allocated
  with malloc() and left uninitialised, so the match search could read stale heap
  contents. On a fresh process the OS supplies zeroed pages and the bug stays
  hidden, but as soon as the allocator recycles a dirty block the search reads
  garbage: the compression ratio becomes unpredictable and the process can crash.
  All three tables are now allocated with calloc(). (lib/lz5hc.c)
- fixed: hashLog3 == 0 (compression levels 1..3, which have no 3-byte hash table)
  still reached code that computed LZ5HC_hash3(u, 0), i.e. a 32-bit shift by 32.
  That is undefined behaviour; on x86 the shift count is masked to 5 bits, which
  yields a huge index and an out-of-bounds write, crashing levels 1-3 on
  LZ5_compress_HC_continue(). Every hashTable3 access is now guarded by
  `hashLog3 != 0`. (lib/lz5hc.c, lib/lz5common.h)
- fixed: LZ5_createStreamHC() never called LZ5_resetStreamHC(), leaving `base` and
  the rest of the context uninitialised; the deferred auto-init in
  LZ5_compressHC_continue_generic() then could not trigger. (lib/lz5hc.c)
- fixed: LZ5F_createCompressionContext() initialised only `version` and `cStage`,
  leaving lz5CtxLevel, lz5CtxPtr, maxBufferSize and tmpBuff with heap garbage.
  (lib/lz5frame.c)
- fixed: negative size arguments were only caught by an unsigned comparison
  trick, which reported them as "input too large" and returned 0 instead of
  rejecting them. LZ5_compress_*_extState(), LZ5_compress_HC_continue(),
  LZ5_compress_destSize_extState(), LZ5_compress_fast_continue(),
  LZ5_decompress_safe(), LZ5_decompress_safe_partial() and
  LZ5_decompress_safe_continue() now test for negative sizes explicitly.
  (lib/lz5.c, lib/lz5hc.c)
- fixed: the encoder's output-limit check estimated the encoded match length as
  (matchLength>>8), which underestimates the real byte count by up to 5 for very
  long matches. olimit is now checked before each length byte is written, so the
  bound is exact and a caller who sized dst exactly can no longer overflow it.
  (lib/lz5.c)
- fixed: LZ5_sizeofState() and LZ5_sizeofStreamState() were declared with an empty
  parameter list instead of (void), which means "unspecified arguments" in C and
  trips -Wstrict-prototypes. (lib/lz5.c)
- fixed: LZ5_decompress_generic() added dictSize to a NULL dictStart, which is
  undefined behaviour even when dictSize is 0. (lib/lz5.c)
- fixed: LZ5F_compressUpdate() did pointer arithmetic on a not-yet-allocated
  tmpBuff. (lib/lz5frame.c)
- fixed: LZ5_compress_generic() added dictSize to a NULL dictionary, and
  subtracted that NULL from source, on the noDict path. Same class of
  undefined behaviour, only reachable on the extended-dictionary code paths.
  (lib/lz5.c)
- fixed: the encoder wrote match[refDelta-1] with refDelta a size_t, which
  underflows to SIZE_MAX when refDelta is 0. The pointer is offset first now.
  (lib/lz5.c)
- fixed: LZ5F_decompress() computed srcBuffer + srcSize and dstBuffer + dstSize
  on possibly-NULL buffers. (lib/lz5frame.c)
- The library now builds and runs clean under AddressSanitizer and
  UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer (previously 4 distinct UB sites). (lib/)
- fixed: LZ5F_compressBound() computed the block count in an `unsigned`, which
  wraps past 4G blocks and returns a bound far too small; LZ5F_compressFrame()
  trusts that bound to decide whether dstBuffer is large enough. (lib/lz5frame.c)
- fixed: LZ5F_compressUpdate() did not check srcSize against LZ5_MAX_INPUT_SIZE
  before handing it to code that narrows size_t to int. (lib/lz5frame.c)
- fixed: the decompression context stored the result of LZ5F_getBlockSize()
  without checking LZ5F_isError(), so a defensive check upstream depended on
  being unreachable. (lib/lz5frame.c)
- fixed: LZ5_saveDictHC() could recompute `base` from a truncated U32 once the
  index space exceeded 4 GB; it now refuses to continue instead. (lib/lz5hc.c)
- fixed: multi-file decompression computed `ifnSize - suffixSize` before checking
  that the name was at least as long as the suffix, underflowing size_t. Also
  checks the malloc() result, like the rest of the file does. (programs/lz5io.c)
- fixed: reading a filename of fewer than 4 characters underflowed
  `strlen(input_filename) - 4`; also added the missing calloc() NULL check.
  (programs/lz5cli.c)
- build: dropped -ffast-math from the default flags. It was also never used
  (FFLAGS is not part of FLAGS), so this is a documentation change; the flag
  remains available through FFLAGS. (programs/Makefile)
- build: `make examples` no longer fails; this source tree ships no examples/
  directory, so the target now says so. (Makefile)
- build: removed test-fuzzer / test-fuzzer32, which referenced a `fuzzer` binary
  that does not exist in this tree. frametest covers the same ground.
  (programs/Makefile)
- build: replaced the dead Travis and AppVeyor configurations with a GitHub
  Actions workflow covering gcc, clang, -Werror, -Wconversion, ASan/UBSan,
  valgrind, macOS and MSVC. (.github/workflows/ci.yml)
- tests: added tests/test_hc_tables.c, a regression test for the table
  initialisation and hashLog3 bugs. It crashes on an unpatched build and is run
  against a poisoned heap (MALLOC_PERTURB_) by `make -C tests test`.

API compatibility, the block format and the frame format are unchanged; data
compressed by 1.5.0 and 1.5.1 is fully interchangeable in both directions.

v1.5
- introduced compatibility with Visual C++ 2010 and newer
- attached Visual Studio 2010 project
- thoroughly tested with 21 Travis CI and 7 AppVeyor CI tests
- fixed bug with reusing a context in lz5frame.c (LZ5F_compressBegin and LZ5_compress_HC_continue)
- fixed rare bug in match finder (concerns levels 4 - 15)

v1.4.1
- fixed bug with a backward match extension (level 11 and 12)

v1.4
- improved: levels from 13 to 15 (maximum compression ratio)
- added a new parser: LZ5HC_optimal_price_bt
- updated documentation: lz5_Block_format.md and lz5_Frame_format.md 
- changed lz5.exe: the "-B" option with block size [1-7] = 64KB, 256KB, 1MB, 4MB, 16MB, 64MB, 256MB (default : 4 = 4MB)
 
v1.3.3
- added: new levels from 11 to 18 (maximum compression ratio)
- added: a new parser: LZ5HC_optimal_price
- fixed: buffer-overflow during decompression (thanks to m^2)

r132
- improved compression ratio
- added: new parsers: LZ5HC_fast, LZ5HC_price_fast, LZ5HC_lowest_price
- added: a special 1-byte codeword for the last occured offset
- added: support for 3-byte long matches (MINMATCH = 3)

r131
The first release based on LZ4 r132 dev
